From: RNSBox <rnsbox@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] riscv: dts: sophgo: use USB gadget mode on the Milk-V Duo 256M

The RNSBox portal exposes a CDC-NCM management interface on the
board's single USB-C port, so the DWC2 controller must run in
peripheral mode.  The EVB DTS already does this.

Also enable saradc: the kernel config carries SOPHGO_CV1800B_ADC for
this board but the node was left disabled.

---
diff --git a/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/sg2002-milkv-duo256m.dts b/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/sg2002-milkv-duo256m.dts
index a2797c0..ac346a3 100644
--- a/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/sg2002-milkv-duo256m.dts
+++ b/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/sg2002-milkv-duo256m.dts
@@ -115,7 +115,11 @@
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+&saradc {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
 &usb {
-	dr_mode = "host";
+	dr_mode = "peripheral";
 	status = "okay";
 };
-- 
2.43.0
